    "body": "  * Errbit version: master\r\n  * OS: Ubuntu 18.04\r\n\r\n#### Steps to reproduce:\r\n\r\n  1. Create a user with malicious name/username in your app\r\n  2. Cause an exception while logged in with that user\r\n  3. Errbit's `notices/_user_attributes` partial executes XSS\r\n\r\n#### Observed Results:\r\n\r\n  * XSS through `.html_safe`-ing attributes (because of Rinku auto link)\r\n\r\n#### Expected Results:\r\n\r\n  * No XSS :)\r\n\r\n#### Cause\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/errbit/errbit/blob/e9ca15b842521d2ae536590c57c3db61fef19a3e/app/views/notices/_user_attributes.html.haml#L10\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how to easily fix this but also keeping autolinking\r\n\r\n#### Example\r\n\r\nThe thankfully friendly attacker delivered an example. The user caused the exception due to a missing length validation but every exception caused by a user might send untrusted data that shouldn't be blindly html_safe'd by errbit\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"user\" => {\r\n    \"name\" => \"\\\"><img src=x onerror=alert('1');> \\\"/><img src=x onerror=prompt(navigator.userAgent)>  \\\"><img/src=\\\"x\\\"/onmouseover=prompt(document.domain);>  \\\"/><svg/onload=prompt(document.domain)>   \\\"><svg/onload=prompt(document.cookie);>  “-prompt`1`-”//  \\\"><svg/onload=alert(document.domain);>  \\\"><svg/onload=prompt(123);>  \\\"><img src=x onerror=prompt(\\\"XSS-Vulnerability\\\");>  /?regionConfirm=alert(document.cookie)});}}%3C/script%3E  \\\"--></style></scRipt><scRipt>alert(\\\"shaniXss\\\")</scRipt>  \\\"></code><svg/onload=prompt(1)>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"783\" alt=\"Errbit — Mysql2::Error: Data too long for column 'name' at row 1 2021-02-13 15-53-36\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/218011/107852942-bb418780-6e13-11eb-9ccb-e4dc3296ebe1.png\">\r\n",
